exercises.hints:
## Hint 1

Three counts means three cases, and the cases are decided by a single
comparison per seed row: not present, present but different, present and
identical. Load the existing rows once, into something you can look up by
code.

## Hint 2

```csharp
var existing = await db.Carriers.ToDictionaryAsync(c => c.Code);
foreach (var seed in V3Db03Seed.Carriers)
{
    if (!existing.TryGetValue(seed.Code, out var row)) { /* insert */ }
    else if (/* differs */) { /* update */ }
    else { /* unchanged */ }
}
await db.SaveChangesAsync();
```

That is one select and one save — two commands, inside your transaction.

## Hint 3

The tracked-entity update is the elegant half: assign the new values to the
loaded row and let change detection decide whether an UPDATE is emitted. But
the gate wants your `updated` count to match what actually changed, so either
compare explicitly or ask the tracker. Both are defensible; one of them
duplicates the framework's work.

