exercises.hints:
## Hint 1

`ValidateOptionsResult` has three shapes: `Success`, `Fail(string)` and
`Fail(IEnumerable<string>)`. The third one is the whole exercise — collect
into a list and return once.

## Hint 2

```csharp
public sealed class MailerValidator : IValidateOptions<MailerOptions>
{
    public ValidateOptionsResult Validate(string? name, MailerOptions o)
    {
        var failures = new List<string>();
        // …
        return failures.Count == 0
            ? ValidateOptionsResult.Success
            : ValidateOptionsResult.Fail(failures);
    }
}
```

Register it as `IValidateOptions<MailerOptions>`; the factory picks up every
registration.

## Hint 3

`ValidateOnStart()` is a separate call from `ValidateDataAnnotations()` and
does something different: it forces the options to be resolved during startup,
so the `OptionsValidationException` becomes a boot failure instead of a 500 on
whichever request first touches the setting. For the endpoint, resolve your
validator from DI and call `Validate(null, candidate)` directly.

